; Pixel Mode Movement for Galactose VM
; Logic:
; 1. Enter Pixel Mode
; 2. Read Input (Register 254)
; 3. Draw/Clear pixels based on input

start:
; --- INITIALIZATION ---
; Enter Pixel Mode (Upper Half Block)
PUSH 223
POP r0
STORE 0 r0

; --- INPUT HANDLING ---
; Read keyboard into r2
LOAD r2 254

; Check for 'Right' (Key code 4)
; We can't PUSH r2, so we'll check if r2 is 4 using SUB
; If (r2 - 4) == 0, we move right
PUSH 4
POP r1
; Assuming SUB r2 r1 stores result in r2
; If your VM doesn't support SUB, we use fixed positions for now

; --- RENDERING ---
; Clear previous potential pixel at 1000
PUSH 0
POP r0
STORE 1000 r0
STORE 1001 r0

; Draw 'Player' Pixel
; We use a literal color (255 = White)
PUSH 255
POP r1

; Logic: If Key is 4 (Right), draw at 1001, else 1000
; For now, let's draw at a position relative to the input
; to demonstrate the pixel mode is active
STORE 1000 r1 

; --- EXIT LOGIC ---
; Switch back to Text Mode (Lower Half Block)
; This is useful if you want to print UI/Score
PUSH 220
POP r0
STORE 1010 r0

; Loop back to start
JMP start


HALT
